# JetBrains Platform
#
# The IntelliJ plugin toolchain, its declared build range, how it finds and launches the language server, and where that range meets the native LSP client feature table.

#>editor_hosts_jetbrains_platform
#:layer #!reference
#:domain #!editor_hosts
#:form #!registry
#:level #!practitioner
#:review #!adversarial_checked
#:valence #!bone
#:era #!current

^"emit"{
 ~#title: "JetBrains Platform"
 ~#claim: "The plugin compiles against WebStorm 2024.2.1, declares builds 242 through 262, and finds its server in two stages: a tool root, then a launch command."
 ~#proof: "Rows cite build.gradle.kts, plugin.xml, SpwLspLauncher.kt, and SpwLspServerSupportProvider.kt at commit 1aa1dc23, and the JetBrains LSP feature table."
 ~#door: "Read the discovery stages, then the token floor row, then the feature radar for the substrate question."
 ~#audience: "maintainers building, verifying, or launching the IntelliJ plugin"
 continuity: "JetBrains Platform | two stages"
 cold_open: "The JetBrains plugin finds its server in two stages, a tool root and then a command, inside one declared build range."
}

